  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a substantive denial that requires an appeal to overturn. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is a valid and often effective next step to challenge the medical necessity and bundling determination. The previous P2P request was likely premature or ineffective because there was no denial on the table at that time; now that a denial exists, this action is procedurally correct.",
